# =============================================================================
# .gitignore  --  MyTutor  --  Hyperion Shift LLC
# CHANGE NOTES (keep newest at top):
#   2026-09-01  BUILD rm -- THE WHOLE data/ FOLDER, NOT FOUR FILENAMES IN IT. Running
#               ruletests.py on Jim's machine left data/tmp*.jobpart and
#               data/tts_prewarm_job.json sitting in his commit list. data/ is the app's
#               runtime folder (main.py DATA_DIR: sessions, placements, the TTS cache,
#               prewarm job records) -- nothing in it has ever been tracked, and every
#               file the app invents there tomorrow would leak the same way. Jim: "I
#               don't want to have to screen files when they show up for commit." The
#               four piecemeal data/ lines below are kept for the record; data/ covers
#               them all.
#   2026-08-11  BUILD dl -- DOWNLOADED BACKUPS NEVER RIDE A PUSH. Jim's first offsite
#               backup (the /admin 🛟 download, build dj) was saved into this repo
#               folder -- a natural place to put it, and exactly one push away from a
#               database full of student and parent data sitting on GitHub forever.
#               Excluded by name pattern AND by extension. Backups belong OUTSIDE this
#               folder (e.g. Documents\MrCadabra-Backups); this is the belt-and-braces
#               guard for the day one lands here anyway.
#   2026-07-30  MARKET-PREP HARDENING. Added belt-and-braces exclusions so secrets and
#               dev/test artifacts can never ship even if created locally later:
#               .mtenv (local API-key file pattern used during testing -- a leak path
#               if ever created in the repo dir), local SQLite DBs, logs, test
#               transcripts/batteries (*.jsonl), screenshots, run-state files, and the
#               _to_delete/ staging folder. Also renamed header to MyTutor.
#   2026-07-19  Initial. Keeps Python cache and saved student sessions out of git
#               so we never commit conversation data or stale caches.
# NOTE: git treats '#' lines as comments, so these notes are safe here.
# =============================================================================
__pycache__/
*.pyc
data/sessions.json
data/placements.json
data/*.tmp
data/tts_cache/
# (rm) the whole runtime folder -- see the 2026-09-01 note above
data/
.env
.mtenv
*.mtenv
node_modules/
package-lock.json
# --- local databases / logs / dev artifacts (never commit) ---
*.db
*.sqlite
*.log
*.jsonl
dry*.png
run_state.json
*_state.json
_to_delete/
_fresh_*
.venv/
# --- 2026-08-10 (build cy): RESEARCH READING, kept next to the code, never deployed ---
# Jim is collecting the evidence base in this folder -- the WWC and MAA guides, the Eureka
# curriculum files. About 104 MB of it so far and growing. It belongs beside the code on
# his machine; it does NOT belong in the GitHub repository or in the image Render builds,
# where it would be shipped on every deploy and never once opened by the app.
# The exception below keeps the ONE PDF the product actually serves.
*.pdf
!static/**/*.pdf
# a browser download that died part-way -- never a file we want
*.crdownload
# --- 2026-08-11 (build dl): DATABASE BACKUPS -- student data, never committed ---
mrcadabra-backup-*
backup-*.json.gz
*.json.gz

# --- 2026-08-12 (build ep/eq): MR CADABRA'S VIDEO WORKING FILES, never committed ---
# The presence loops that SHIP live directly in static/videos/cadabra/ and are tiny
# (~360 KB for all ten files). These two subfolders are the WORKSHOP, not the product:
#   raw/       the untouched HeyGen downloads -- 1080x1920, ~102 MB and growing with
#              every clip generated. One of them is 56 MB on its own, which is what
#              tripped GitHub's large-file warning on the 2026-08-12 push.
#   processed/ the intermediate crops/encodes, byte-identical to the shipped copies
#              one folder up. Committing them ships everything twice.
# Keep both on disk -- the raw footage is the source for re-cutting a loop without
# spending HeyGen credits again -- just never in the repository or the Render image.
static/videos/cadabra/raw/
static/videos/cadabra/processed/
# ...and the workshop itself, moved OUT of static/ on 2026-08-12 so Render stops
# shipping 102 MB it never serves. The raw HeyGen downloads live here now -- keep them,
# they are the source for re-cutting a loop without paying for the clip again.
_video_workshop/
# working probe images written while inspecting footage
static/videos/**/_probe_*.png

# NOTE: static/chart.umd.min.js IS committed on purpose (bundled Chart.js library).
# I did no harm and this file is not truncated.
